## 📊 Step-by-Step Execution & Verification Loop

Follow this explicit terminal loop sequence on the cluster manager host terminal (`jump-host`) to deploy and verify the data transmission integrity layer:

```bash
# 1. Apply the manifest file to build the resource layer
kubectl apply -f pod-volume-share.yaml

# 2. Monitor container ready states until status marks move to Running
kubectl get pod volume-share-datacenter

# 3. Interactively execute into the first container to create the data payload file
kubectl exec -it volume-share-datacenter -c volume-container-datacenter-1 -- /bin/sh -c "echo 'Welcome to xFusionCorp Industries' > /tmp/official/official.txt"

# 4. Interactively execute into the second container to cross-verify the file sync state
kubectl exec -it volume-share-datacenter -c volume-container-datacenter-2 -- cat /tmp/games/official.txt
```

